From: Kieran Drewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] output-shield: drop the animation before the rest on finalize

When an output is destroyed while its shield animation is still running,
finalizing the shield crashes:

  phoc_bling_unmap: assertion failed: (PHOC_IS_BLING (self))

finalize clears the color rect before the animation. Dropping the last
reference to a running animation skips it to the end, which emits
::done, and the shield's handler then calls stop_render() with the
color rect already gone.

This happens on every session pause (suspend, VT switch) when a disabled
output is present: wlroots destroys all connected outputs on pause, and
an animation started on an output that never renders a frame never
finishes. On the Pixel 4a (5G) the disabled writeback output Virtual-1
triggers it:

  #6  phoc_bling_unmap (self=0x0) at ../src/bling.c:79
  #7  stop_render at ../src/output-shield.c:143
  #12 phoc_timed_animation_skip at ../src/anim/timed-animation.c:479
  #14 phoc_animation_dispose at ../src/anim/timed-animation.c:251
  #16 phoc_output_shield_finalize at ../src/output-shield.c:244
  #18 phoc_output_finalize at ../src/output.c:1143
  #25 drm_connector_destroy_output (Virtual-1)
  #26 handle_session_active at backend/drm/backend.c:120

Disconnect from the animation and drop it first.

---
--- a/src/output-shield.c
+++ b/src/output-shield.c
@@ -236,12 +236,19 @@
 {
   PhocOutputShield *self = PHOC_OUTPUT_SHIELD (object);
 
+  /* Drop the animation first. Disposing a running animation skips it to
+   * the end, which emits ::done; with the handler still connected that
+   * would call stop_render() on a half finalized shield. An animation can
+   * still be running here when the output never rendered a frame (e.g. a
+   * disabled output destroyed on session pause). */
+  g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_data (self->animation, self);
+  g_clear_object (&self->animation);
+
   set_output (self, NULL);
   stop_render (self);
 
   g_clear_object (&self->color_rect);
   g_clear_object (&self->easer);
-  g_clear_object (&self->animation);
   g_clear_object (&self->spinner);
 
   G_OBJECT_CLASS (phoc_output_shield_parent_class)->finalize (object);
